From: SP11 audio worker <audio-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH candidate] ASoC: qcom: report speaker graph setup metadata

Report graph-management return codes, private supplement SET_CFG parameter
IDs and return codes, the VI graph DMA format and mask, VI speaker and map
counts, map entries, each feedback slave's requested port and mask, and
a direct PA-enable register read when the codec is already active.
Do not log calibration values or capture samples. A successful SET_CFG is
an APM command acknowledgment, not proof of the algorithm or sense data.

These messages describe requested configuration, not SoundWire slot
assignment on the wire. They add no route, value, mute or guard bypass.

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@
 	struct apm_graph_mgmt_cmd *mgmt_cmd;
 	struct audioreach_sub_graph *sg;
 	struct q6apm *apm = graph->apm;
-	int i = 0, payload_size = APM_GRAPH_MGMT_PSIZE(mgmt_cmd, num_sub_graphs);
+	int ret, i = 0, payload_size = APM_GRAPH_MGMT_PSIZE(mgmt_cmd, num_sub_graphs);
 
 	struct gpr_pkt *pkt __free(kfree) = audioreach_alloc_apm_cmd_pkt(payload_size, opcode, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(pkt))
@@ -132,7 +132,9 @@
 	list_for_each_entry(sg, &info->sg_list, node)
 		mgmt_cmd->sub_graph_id_list[i++] = sg->sub_graph_id;
 
-	return q6apm_send_cmd_sync(apm, pkt, 0);
+	ret = q6apm_send_cmd_sync(apm, pkt, 0);
+	dev_info(apm->dev, "graph %u command=0x%08x rc=%d\n", graph->id, opcode, ret);
+	return ret;
 }
 
